<title>UK: Virtuality H1 pre-tax loss deepens.</title>
<headline>Virtuality H1 pre-tax loss deepens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr loss (pence)	 13.4		   vs 2.2</p>
<p> Pretax loss		3.78		   vs 0.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   3.54		   vs 6.27</p>
<p> Operating loss	   3.76		   vs 0.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Virtual reality systems and technology firm Virtuality Group Plc said that no dividend will be paid. It also said that its previous forecast for the second half of the year made in July now looks to be optimistic. Virtuality said in July that full year revenue growth would be similar to last year.  </p>
<p>Virtuality shares were down sharply at 145p by 0747 GMT from yesterday's close of 206-1/2p.</p>
</text>
